	 <note id="GUID-99A7F778-4333-4B30-AAA0-24952EBC795A"> Preliminary values and subject to change. 
		<p> 
		  <sup>1</sup> NVL and PTL DF, Ψ<sub>sn -hp</sub> , and Ψ<sub>hp-a</sub> are calculated using Intel Technology Targets based on most up to date test data. 
		</p> 
		<p> 
		  <sup>2</sup> Positive values mean heat exchanger performance needs to increase for this generation; negative values means last generation's heat exchanger will have thermal margin if reused. 
		</p> 
		<p> 
		  <sup>3</sup> Resistances calculated based on the same thermal solution assumptions used for PTL. 
		</p> 
		<p> 
		  <sup>4</sup> DF<sub>Thermal_Solution</sub> is different from the Global DF, refer to the 
		  <xref scope="local" format="dita" href="GUID-1D89D292-7CD3-4E06-9D28-4E18877EC4E0.dita"><?xm-replace_text Calculating Mobile Cooling Needs at Target PL1 (1)?></xref> for definition. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>5</sup> DF<sub>Thermal_Solution</sub> is sensitive to the nature of the workload, Ψ<sub>sn-hp</sub> and Ψ<sub>hp-a</sub> are less sensitive to the nature of workload. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>6</sup> There are changes in cooling needs based on silicon measurements. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup> 7</sup> The thermal solution used is 1.3mm cold plate soldered to 3 heat pipes (2nos. of original diameter of 6mm crushed to 1.6mm, 1no. of original diameter of 8mm crushed to 1.6mm) 
		</p> 
		<p> 
		  <sup>8</sup> The thermal solution used is 3mm cold plate soldered to 2 heat pipes (1no. of original diameter of 8mm crushed to 2mm, 1no. of original diameter of 10mm crushed to 2mm). 
		</p> 
	 </note> 
